 #### Scenario: Independent normal comparison baseline
 - **WHEN** The same admitted factorial/list/tree or pending-caller state is materialized without caching, with cold caches and with warm caches.
 - **THEN** Stable dependency ordering and explicit bindings produce identical decoded reference prefixes, ordered frames/environments, outcomes and reference-work observations against independently authored expectations. Cache/lifetime/streaming variants retain the uncached baseline; reusable keys include exact program/profile/layout and immutable inputs, while helper visits, copies, live values and memory remain separate diagnostics. Neither those expectations nor semantic behavior are generated from the materializer/DAG metadata.
+
+### October 19 adopted nominal body-typed profile refinement
+
+Root adopted the three nominal static judgments on October 19 after two Opus
+opinions and a fresh Muse applicability amendment review. This scoped refinement
+uses existing UIREQ traces; the original 35 clauses, revision03, additive
+requirements and all retained exits remain unchanged. The source-review stopping point had all new checks UNRUN. Root later observed
+separate BW27 and NW21 qualification; that scoped validation is not requirement
+closure. See the [tracked adoption summary](../../../../../docs/sherlock/reference/nominal-body-compiler-adoption-20261019.md).
+
+#### UIREQ-002 / UIREQ-027 scenario: Truthful public body completion
+- **WHEN** a caller selects the public body-typed nominal compiler.
+- **THEN** bounded parse SHALL precede first owner type preparation with the exact supplied layout/domain; all bodies and closed entry SHALL pass before the unchanged program enters actual owner admission and genesis. The report SHALL wrap the unchanged raw report and identify completed adopted judgments without first-preparation type IDs. Parse, first Preparation, BodyType, OwnerAdmission and Genesis SHALL retain distinct original typed payloads.
+
+#### UIREQ-009 / UIREQ-006 scenario: Nominal structural equality typing
+- **WHEN** both Eq operands individually typecheck.
+- **THEN** body typing SHALL produce Bool whether or not their canonical types agree; an illtyped operand SHALL retain its error. This judgment supplies no runtime observation or correspondence theorem.
+
+#### UIREQ-027 scenario: Every declaration and repeated parameter
+- **WHEN** body typing visits declarations, including unused and later same-named declarations.
+- **THEN** it SHALL use fresh declared parameter contexts and signature references without unrolling calls; a repeated parameter SHALL fail at its second binder, consistent with owner V4. First-match isolated signature lookup SHALL not bypass owner V3's duplicate-function rejection.
+
+#### UIREQ-007 / UIREQ-008 scenario: Every arm has distinct binders
+- **WHEN** any arm repeats a source-preorder binder, including an unselected or dedicated-only unplanned arm.
+- **THEN** body typing SHALL reject it while permitting separate-arm name reuse and outer lexical shadowing. The diagnostic SHALL retain its typed name and arm-body source path. This restricts the raw owner language's never-selectable repeated dedicated arms and supplies neither exhaustiveness nor general reachability analysis.
+
+#### UIREQ-002 / UIREQ-027 scenario: Explicit selected body-typed nominal command
+- **WHEN** `mori compile` explicitly selects `moriarty-sherlock-nominal-body-typed/1` with the existing execution profile, explicit config and closed entry.
+- **THEN** its actual selected handler SHALL call the adopted public body wrapper using the same config layout/domain and owned source; it SHALL report completed judgments only after the full body check passes, preserve all five original program-failure payloads with exact optional locations, and publish only after preparation/serialization. Later publication errors SHALL preserve completed body metadata while runtime completion stays false. The structural nominal profile SHALL retain not-performed body qualification. At source freeze these21 new handler tests were UNRUN. Root later observed the exact NW normal Core/real-handler24 cut pass; BW27 remains a separate result. Neither closes the requirement.
